  'filament a print uses is picked in the project, so when someone says what they loaded there is nothing to save.\n';

const connecting = (adding: boolean) =>
  'Rules for connecting a printer:\n' +
  '- The connection tools act on the printer this is about, named below; a printer found on the network is only ever ' +
  'a deviceId.\n' +
  `- Connecting is optional${adding ? OFFER_AFTER_ADDING : ''}. For a Bambu Lab printer, start with printer_connection_status; ` +
  'the app then adds what its states mean and the next step for each. For Moonraker or OctoPrint, ask for the address they ' +
  'open it with in a browser, including its port when there is one, then call printer_connect.\n' +
  '- Never ask for a password, access code or API key in chat, and never repeat one: printer_connect opens a local form ' +
  'where the person types it. When the tool reports credential_requested, say briefly to use that form.\n' +
  '- After the form is submitted, the app checks the printer for about 30 seconds. Answer anything the person says meanwhile; the app\'s ' +
  'note says how it went. A failure that is a timeout means no response, not a wrong code.\n' +
  '- After a failed connection, say what the app saw in the person\'s terms and work out why. Whenever they would ' +
  'rather stop, they can leave it for now, as they can prepare prints ' +
  'for it without a connection. If they ' +
  'leave it, say again that they can prepare prints for it, that Connect… in its menu on Home is there for later, and that ' +
  'they can close this chat now.\n';

const FINISHING =
  'Rules for finishing:\n' +
  '- Once nothing is left to decide, say what that leaves them with and that it is safe to close this chat now. ' +
  'Do not add a Choices line. That is after the person turns down connecting, after the app says the connection ' +
        return;
    }
    m_connecting = name;
    m_last_look  = {};
    m_host.session_changed();
}

void PrinterConversation::connection_failed(const std::string& message_id)
{
    // The rule is the app's, not the model's: a model that is stuck is the one
    // least likely to say so. Only where there is a skill a report can improve.
    if (++m_failed_connections != 2 || !connection_skill())
        return;
    const json report{{"report", "connection"},
                      {"trigger", "failed_twice"},
                      {"connectionType", "bambu"},
                      {"model", saved(m_printer_name).model},
                      {"chat", without_secrets(m_host.chat_record())}};
    m_blocks.push_back(json{{"id", next_block_id()}, {"seq", m_blocks.size() + 1}, {"afterMessageId", message_id},
                            {"kind", "report"}, {"report", report.dump(2)}});
    m_host.post_note("The app is asking the person, on a card of its own, whether to send a report of this chat to the JusPrin "
                     "developers. Nothing is sent unless they choose to.");
}

void PrinterConversation::answer_report(const std::string& block_id, bool send)
{
    for (json& block : m_blocks) {
        if (block.value("id", std::string()) != block_id || block.value("kind", std::string()) != "report" || block.contains("answer"))
            continue;
        if (send) {
            const std::string kept = m_backend.keep_connection_report(block.at("report").get<std::string>());
            block["answer"] = kept.empty() ? "failed" : "kept";
